          "delegation_record_id": null,
          "blocked_since_utc": "2026-07-20T21:00:00Z",
          "unblock_criteria": "ESC-EXEC-20260720-01 resolved with a disposition of (a) single-provider reframe, (b) defer to future cycle, or (c) explicit accept-as-specified from Product Owner",
          "completed_utc": null,
          "acceptance_verified": false,
          "spec_references": ["docs/design/2026-07-20__release-v7.6/consolidated-ai-cost-view/ux_spec.md"],
          "spec_reference_not_applicable": false,
          "spec_reference_not_applicable_reason": null,
          "deviations_filed": false,
          "last_completed_substep": null,
          "sign_off_record": null,
          "notes": "Reclassified autonomous -> delegated_decision mid-sprint (LL-v2.3-EX-02 pattern, in reverse). Original classification assumed Gemini and Claude are two genuinely separate cost-generating AI providers per the PO-approved UX spec's premise. Tracing gemini_service.py's actual implementation found it exclusively calls the Anthropic Claude API (_call_claude(), MODEL_VERSION='claude-haiku-4-5') -- no Gemini API integration exists anywhere in the codebase (verified: no GEMINI_API_KEY, no google-generativeai package, no genai import). Every Claude call dual-writes to gemini_audit_log AND claude_audit_log for the same spend event -- confirmed independently by docs/ops/gemini_cost_tracking.md's own H1 heading ('Claude API Cost Tracking') and docs/ops/claude_cost_review_2026-05.md §1. Implementing the story literally would double-count one real cost stream as two providers' spend -- a correctness/quality defect, not a UI question the engine can resolve alone. Escalated as ESC-EXEC-20260720-01 (Quality trigger, execution_escalations.md) with 3 proposed resolution options. Does not block other EPICs -- continuing to EPIC-08."
        }
      }
    },
